msgid "`print` is fine while you develop. A script that runs every month needs a **log**: lines with a time and a level, in a file, that you can read when something went wrong. The module `logging` comes with Python:"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/09-errors-and-files.md:1342
msgid "The **levels**, from the least to the most serious: `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`, `CRITICAL`. `level=logging.INFO` writes INFO and above; switch to `DEBUG` when you look for a problem, without changing the code. Use `%s` placeholders, not f-strings, in log messages - the text is built only if the line is written. (`force=True` replaces an earlier setup; in a script you call `basicConfig` once, at the start.)"
