#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/09-errors-and-files.md:1416
msgid "Sort the files by the month in their name, not by the name itself. When is that different? (Hint: `payments_2026-10.csv` and `payments_2026-9.csv`.)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/09-errors-and-files.md:1420
msgid "Inside the `with`: `values = [to_float(row[\"amount\"]) for row in csv.DictReader(file)]`, then `totals[month] = sum(v for v in values if v is not None)` and `skipped[path.name] = values.count(None)`. The `UnicodeDecodeError` still needs the `try`."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/09-errors-and-files.md:1424
msgid "`sorted(folder.glob(...), key=lambda p: tuple(int(x) for x in re.search(r\"(\\d{4})-(\\d{1,2})\", p.name).groups()))`. Sorting by name puts `2026-10` before `2026-9`, because text is compared letter by letter - another reason for two-digit months in file names."
